                    insight_sustained:      `Sustained & reset the norm: Priya delivered NorthPeak AND came through with her health intact — and she turned a private boundary into a team standard that protects all seven reports. You fixed the identity, not just the calendar.`,
                    insight_burnout:        `Delivered but burning out: the sprint shipped, but Priya ends it under the well-being floor and in the quit-risk band. A second consecutive high-demand episode is the single strongest predictor she resigns within six months — a hollow win.`,
                    insight_clientrisk:     `Protected self, client at risk: Priya's well-being held, but segmentation taken too far put the NorthPeak relationship and the sprint in jeopardy. Well-being and performance aren't a binary — bounded flexibility was the missing move.`,
                    insight_mixed:          `Mixed result: the boundaries only half-held. Somewhere the plan fought Priya's style, an unenforced limit taught the client it was negotiable, or the identity went unaddressed and the behaviour crept back.`,
                    insight_quitrisk:       `Well-being ended in the burnout band — the strongest predictor of resignation within six months. Whatever the headline result, an exhausted high performer who leaves takes the client relationship with her.`,
                    insight_lowcred:        `Boundary credibility stayed low: Priya announced limits she didn't hold, so the client and team learned they were negotiable. Unenforced boundaries are worse than none.`,
                    insight_solofix:        `The team norm never moved: Priya solved for herself and left the seven reports modelling an always-on lead. Individual boundary work that doesn't scale to the team leaves the disease in place.`,
                    insight_wentdark:       `Going dark on a real board-deadline risk damaged the client relationship Priya personally owns. Protecting home perfectly can create a new failure — the bounded exception exists for exactly that moment.`,
                    insight_lasts:          `This is change that lasts: well-being, performance, credible boundaries and a healthier team norm all moving together. The boundary survives the sprint and resets the standard for everyone watching.`,

                    hint_burnout:           `Priya is ending the sprint in the burnout band — the strongest predictor she quits. Protect well-being now: a credible non-negotiable, real delegation, and an enforced cadence.`,
                    hint_credibility:       `Boundary credibility is dangerously low — she's announcing limits she doesn't hold. Reset “real-time” explicitly and enforce what she announces, or the client learns her limits are negotiable.`,
                    hint_wellbeing:         `Well-being is critically low. Close the demand-capacity gap through delegation and a workable cadence — working harder will not move this number.`,
                    hint_team:              `The seven reports still model an always-on lead. Turn Priya's boundary into a team norm — async-by-default and a rotating on-call she models herself.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — well-being, performance and team norm all healthy. Lock it in with leading indicators so it survives past the sprint.`,

